{"ts": "2026-11-05T07:33:50.715139Z", "run_id": "r-20261105T0732Z-bd14", "unit": "openspec:add-mock-test-runs", "seq": 16, "type": "delegate.result", "question": "Q-001", "id": "Q-001", "status": "answered", "reason": "The two scenarios only share the first setup clause; the WHENs diverge and the THENs assert on disjoint route families (runs routes vs the test route under flows). The repository shows \"exactly five run routes\" is scoped to /api/v1/runs by the existing test's filter, the unit's modified flow-registry spec explicitly expects the extra test route on main's public server, and main.ts already registers run routes after launchDurable, so Decision 7's wiring satisfies both. No business decision is needed; the documents settle it.", "called": true, "tasks": ["1.1", "1.2", "2.1", "2.2", "3.1", "4.1", "4.2", "5.1"], "target": null, "kind": "ambiguous", "profile": "delegate-fable", "model": "claude-fable-5-1", "cli": "claude-code", "cost_usd": 1.2141305, "decision": "answer", "answer_sha256": "e6a4cc2dbc4374d3b3e61704c2ce69c1254998f8bf84bdc4470db4494b1b4ea3", "checked": [{"ref": "src/main.runs.test.ts:191", "quote": "const runRoutes = publicRoutes.filter(", "claim": "The runs-api wiring test counts exactly five routes only among those under /api/v1/runs, so the test route under /api/v1/flows does not break it."}, {"ref": "openspec/specs/runs-api/spec.md:86", "quote": "and no `POST /api/v1/runs`; `unregisteredRouteErrors` over the routes is `[]`", "claim": "The runs-api THEN asserts on the run routes and the absence of POST /api/v1/runs, not on the absence of flow routes."}, {"ref": "spec:specs/flow-registry/spec.md#scenario-the-route-table-and-the-real-engine", "quote": "the public server of `main` defines the same seven routes and one more, `POST /api/v1/flows/:flowId/versions/:hash/test` with action `test_flow`", "claim": "This unit's own spec expects main's first no-database run to define the test route alongside the existing routes, so both scenarios describe one route table."}, {"ref": "spec:design.md#decisions", "quote": "directly after U36's `registerRunRoutes(...)`: `registerTestRunRoutes(server, { pool, clock: systemClock, ids: systemIds, interpreter })`", "claim": "The design places the test route registration after the run routes, after the launch and before the listener, so both wiring scenarios are satisfied by one main."}, {"ref": "src/main.ts:277", "quote": "registerRunRoutes(server, {", "claim": "main already registers the run routes after the launchDurable call at line 263, the insertion point Decision 7 names."}, {"ref": "src/main.flows.test.ts:150", "quote": "const flowRoutes = publicRoutes.filter((route) => route.url.startsWith(\"/api/v1/flows\"));", "claim": "The flow-route wiring test likewise scopes its exact count to routes under /api/v1/flows, confirming the per-family reading of \"exactly\"."}]}
